        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "p",
         "text": "Why it matters",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "h2",
         "text": "What Makes a Good Realtor Logo in Austin?",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<p>A good real estate logo is legible at a distance, simple enough to recognize at a glance and distinct from the brokerage marks around it. Your logo lives on a sign in a front yard in Mueller, a rider on a lot in Leander, a postcard in a Westlake mailbox and a tiny square on Instagram. If it only looks good large, it is not doing its job.</p><p>Austin also has a lot of agents. Rooftop icons, keys and generic skylines blur together. We look at your farm area, your price point and the competition, then design something that fits you, whether that is a clean monogram for a luxury team or a friendly wordmark for a first-time-buyer specialist.</p>",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "list",
         "items": [
          {
           "text": "Strong contrast so the name reads from a moving car",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "A compact icon or monogram for social and favicon use",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "Works alongside your brokerage branding where required",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          }
         ],
         "classes": []
        }
       ]
      },
