    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": "p",
     "text": "Local answers",
     "classes": []
    },
    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": "h2",
     "text": "Where Can I Get a Real Estate Logo Designed in Austin?",
     "align": "left",
     "classes": []
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "html": "<p>Logo Design Austin works with agents and brokerages across Austin and the surrounding suburbs, fully online. You do not need to book a meeting room or drive across town; a designer talks with you by phone or text and sends concepts you can review between appointments.</p><h3>Luxury and listing-agent logos in Westlake (78746) and Tarrytown (78703)</h3><p>Higher-end markets usually call for restraint: a refined serif or monogram, a limited palette and plenty of white space. That style reads as confident on a rider in Westlake Hills or a brochure for a Tarrytown listing.</p><h3>Team and brokerage logos near the Domain (78758) and in Round Rock (78664)</h3><p>Growing teams in North Austin and Williamson County often need a logo that can carry several agent names and still look unified on group signage, a recruiting page and a shared Instagram account.</p><h3>Property management and investor logos in East Austin (78702) and Mueller (78723)</h3><p>Leasing and management companies need marks that look dependable on lease paperwork, a resident portal and a building sign. We design versions for both residents and owners.</p><h3>How much does a real estate logo cost in Austin?</h3><p>A custom real estate logo at Logo Design Austin is priced from $125 to $175, depending on complexity. There is no upfront charge; you review concepts, request revisions and pay when you are satisfied. Signs, cards and social templates can be added afterward.</p>",
     "align": "left",
     "classes": []
    },
