      },
      {
       "t": "heading",
       "level": "h2",
       "text": "Real Estate Logo Design FAQs",
       "align": "center",
       "classes": []
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "accordion",
     "items": [
      {
       "q": "Can I use my own logo if my brokerage has its own branding?",
       "a": "<p>Often yes, but rules vary. Many brokerages allow a personal or team logo as long as the brokerage name and logo also appear with equal or greater prominence. Check your brokerage's brand guidelines and we will design within them.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "What colors work best for a real estate logo?",
       "a": "<p>Navy, charcoal, deep green and black read as trustworthy and print well on signs. A single accent color helps you stand out. We test contrast so the logo stays readable on white sign panels and dark social backgrounds.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Should a realtor logo include a house or roof icon?",
       "a": "<p>It can, but rooftops are very common. A monogram, a distinctive wordmark or a symbol tied to your area often makes you more memorable. We usually show both directions so you can compare.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "How much does a real estate logo cost in Austin?",
       "a": "<p>Custom logo design at Logo Design Austin is priced from $125 to $175, depending on complexity, with no upfront payment. You pay after you approve the final design.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "How fast can I get a logo for my new listing signs?",
       "a": "<p>First concepts the same day are often possible for straightforward projects after review. Final timing depends on revisions and how quickly you send feedback.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "What files will I receive for signs and my website?",
       "a": "<p>You get vector files (AI, EPS, SVG and PDF) for sign shops and printers, plus high-resolution PNGs with transparent backgrounds for your website, IDX pages, email signature and social profiles.</p>"
      }
     ],
     "classes": []
    }
   ]
